WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.840 --> 00:00:04.710
The heroes of Wayne on YouTube Premium go
on one wild journey over the course of the

00:00:04.710 --> 00:00:06.160
show's rollicking first season.

00:00:06.390 --> 00:00:09.500
Where do their adventures leave them, and
what might happen to them next?

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:11.280
This is the ending of Wayne explained.

00:00:11.560 --> 00:00:14.880
Before you start watching the series, the
name Wayne makes the show sound like it could

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:16.400
be about basically anything.

00:00:16.610 --> 00:00:20.060
But by the time the first season is over,
it feels like a title that tells you all you

00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:20.760
need to know.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:22.000
What's the show about?

00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:27.150
Well, it's about that kid Wayne, that absolute
madman, the Robin Hood-meets-Dirty Harry of

00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:28.260
Brockton, Massachusetts.

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:29.780
How else could you describe it?

00:00:30.140 --> 00:00:31.120
"Who's that?"

00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:32.920
"That's f---in' Wayne."

00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:37.720
Neither hero nor anti-hero, the protagonist
of Wayne is more like a force of nature, a

00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:40.660
teenage dispenser of violent justice whose
reputation precedes him.

00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:44.620
Everywhere he goes, his legend grows, with
his enemies being left bruised, bloodied,

00:00:44.620 --> 00:00:48.220
or — in the case of Del's daddy — with
their nose half-bitten off.

00:00:48.740 --> 00:00:52.260
But no matter how mythical Wayne is, he's
far from the show's only focus.

00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:54.960
The second half of the equation is his classmate
Del.

00:00:55.240 --> 00:00:58.000
Which is definitely not short for nothing,
so don't ask.

00:00:58.460 --> 00:00:59.640
"Delilah!

00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:01.840
Delilah!"

00:01:02.180 --> 00:01:06.439
The two teens are bonded by a traumatic home
life, social outcast status, and a tendency

00:01:06.440 --> 00:01:09.460
to talk with the heaviest Boston accents in
the history of the east coast.

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:12.660
"I don't think it's got good-for-you stuff
in it, like vitamins and all that.

00:01:13.900 --> 00:01:15.259
Like orange juice and pretzels."

00:01:15.259 --> 00:01:16.259
"Pretzels don't got vitamins."

00:01:16.260 --> 00:01:17.240
"I'm pretty sure they do."

00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:17.740
"Right.

00:01:18.140 --> 00:01:19.140
Pretzel vitamins."

00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:23.200
Wayne and Del spend the majority of the season
making their way down the east coast to Ocala,

00:01:23.210 --> 00:01:27.500
Florida, supposedly for the purpose of retrieving
a gold Trans Am that used to belong to Wayne's

00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:28.220
late father.

00:01:28.620 --> 00:01:32.369
The car is the closest thing Wayne has to
a birthright, being put together with real

00:01:32.369 --> 00:01:36.160
passion by his dad before it was lost to Wayne's
absentee mother, Maureen.

00:01:36.520 --> 00:01:40.000
Since then, it's ended up in the possession
of Curtis and Reggie, the hellishly criminal

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:42.840
father and son duo she ends up living with
down south.

00:01:43.189 --> 00:01:46.840
At the start of the series, getting the car
back makes for such a thin motivation to cross

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:49.880
the country that it almost feels like a part
of the show's big joke.

00:01:50.329 --> 00:01:54.499
But when Wayne and Del actually arrive in
Ocala near the season's end, it quickly becomes

00:01:54.499 --> 00:01:58.169
clear to Del that Wayne came all this way
for reasons more emotional than he at first

00:01:58.169 --> 00:01:58.660
revealed.

00:01:59.120 --> 00:02:01.940
He doesn't just want a family heirloom — he
wants family.

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:06.600
If he can get the Trans Am back from Reggie,
his dirtbag stepbrother — if you can even

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:08.440
really call him that — then all the better.

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:13.160
As capable as he is on his own, Wayne is still
just a teenager looking for somewhere to belong.

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:17.450
He's so desperate for it that he'd drive across
the country to seek affection and acceptance

00:02:17.450 --> 00:02:20.069
from the mother who abandoned him when he
was only five.

00:02:20.069 --> 00:02:23.989
So what if she lives in, as Del calls it,
"a white trash fortress of meth-heads and

00:02:23.989 --> 00:02:24.600
crocodiles"?

00:02:24.980 --> 00:02:28.600
After Wayne's dad dies, she and her horrid
new family are all he has left.

00:02:29.480 --> 00:02:30.180
"Oh my God.

00:02:30.260 --> 00:02:34.420
I'm sorry, do you not care about how your
son's been doing for the past 11 g------ years?"

00:02:35.480 --> 00:02:37.860
"Has it been 11 g------ years?"

00:02:38.320 --> 00:02:40.660
Wayne never talks about any of this, of course.

00:02:40.670 --> 00:02:45.069
Though he's not what you'd call nervous around
people, Wayne is a definite introvert, keeping

00:02:45.069 --> 00:02:47.880
his emotions and thoughts guarded at pretty
much all times.

00:02:48.020 --> 00:02:52.159
Arriving with Del in Florida is the first
time that he really shows any vulnerability,

00:02:52.160 --> 00:02:56.020
and his mother's such a terrible person that
the effort doesn't really pay off.

00:02:56.300 --> 00:03:00.030
At the start of the show, many of Wayne's
Brockton-based antagonists, like police Sergeant

00:03:00.030 --> 00:03:04.040
Geller and Del's dad and brothers see only
malicious evil in Wayne's behavior.

00:03:04.290 --> 00:03:07.980
They make assumptions of his character, based
on the trail of broken bones and blood he

00:03:07.980 --> 00:03:09.340
tends to leave behind him.

00:03:09.650 --> 00:03:13.340
As they follow his tracks toward Florida,
Wayne's pursuers think that he's a madman

00:03:13.340 --> 00:03:14.260
in a bad way.

00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:18.420
At first, they figure he kidnapped Del — a
somewhat reasonable assumption, considering

00:03:18.420 --> 00:03:21.260
the barbaric level of damage he inflicted
on Del's family.

00:03:21.440 --> 00:03:25.220
But when they start asking questions to the
people who've met Wayne, and stayed on his

00:03:25.220 --> 00:03:28.560
good side, they uncover a different take on
the fugitive teen.

00:03:28.920 --> 00:03:33.460
Wayne is feared by his enemies, sure — but
he's motivated solely by a desire to do good.

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:38.420
"No matter how bad life
treated you or betrayed you, from where I'm

00:03:38.420 --> 00:03:43.140
sitting, everything you do, it's done out
of love."

00:03:43.380 --> 00:03:47.320
The source of Wayne's chaotic good nature
comes out in Ocala, when Wayne is catching

00:03:47.320 --> 00:03:50.700
up with his mother and her new family for
the first time in more than a decade.

00:03:51.049 --> 00:03:55.160
We learn from Mo's recollections that Wayne
is following in the footsteps of his father,

00:03:55.160 --> 00:03:57.800
who was something of a hometown legend himself
as a younger man.

00:03:57.800 --> 00:04:02.120
Wayne's father, Mo explains, always had a
certain code of honor, along with a notorious

00:04:02.120 --> 00:04:05.140
intensity known to drive neighbors out of
town.

00:04:05.140 --> 00:04:08.170
Everything was always black and white with
him, she says — right or wrong, with no

00:04:08.170 --> 00:04:08.840
middle ground.

00:04:08.980 --> 00:04:10.380
Sure sounds familiar, doesn't it?

00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:14.980
Just like that, we finally learn almost everything
we need to know about why Wayne is the way

00:04:14.980 --> 00:04:15.660
he is.

00:04:16.020 --> 00:04:20.220
It's a little bit of nature, and a little
bit of nurture — or the lack thereof.

00:04:20.280 --> 00:04:24.180
At the end of the show's first season, Wayne
and Del's trail of destruction finally catches

00:04:24.180 --> 00:04:24.700
up with them.

00:04:24.900 --> 00:04:28.580
Sergeant Geller manages to arrest Wayne, with
arrangements being made to send him back to

00:04:28.580 --> 00:04:30.380
Brockton to face the justice system.

00:04:30.650 --> 00:04:34.560
Del tries to escape with Wayne, but her father
and brothers catch up with them too, stopping

00:04:34.570 --> 00:04:38.229
them in their tracks and successfully shepherding
her away from him, whether she likes it or

00:04:38.229 --> 00:04:38.720
not.

00:04:38.740 --> 00:04:42.620
The season seems to end with both protagonists
at a personal low, having been captured by

00:04:42.620 --> 00:04:44.560
everything they were trying to run away from.

00:04:44.930 --> 00:04:49.000
Del is back with her terrible family, and
Wayne is incarcerated, probably not for the

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:50.020
last time in his life.

00:04:50.240 --> 00:04:54.260
But while their physical circumstances at
the season's end may be less than ideal, both

00:04:54.260 --> 00:04:57.960
characters have grown emotionally, becoming
better people than they've ever been before.

00:04:58.250 --> 00:05:02.440
On a personal level, Wayne ends the last episode
in an almost triumphant place.

00:05:02.440 --> 00:05:06.080
After the death of his father, he migrated
south to see if he could find a new home with

00:05:06.080 --> 00:05:06.760
family there.

00:05:07.080 --> 00:05:10.980
Instead, they all took turns trying to kill
each other while his mother sipped wine.

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:12.900
Now Wayne knows what the real score is.

00:05:13.120 --> 00:05:14.800
His future's not with family.

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:16.580
His salvation is with Del.

